    "details": "X.Org reports:\n\n> Multiple issues have been found in the X client library\n> implementations published by X.Org for which we are releasing security\n> fixes for.\n>\n> - CVE-2026-93541: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XQueryDeviceState()\n> - CVE-2026-93542: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XI2 class parsing via\n>   size_classes() and copy_classes()\n> - CVE-2026-93543: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XI2 class parser\n> - CVE-2026-93544: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XI2 XIQueryDevice\n>   reply parsing\n> - CVE-2026-93545: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XListInputDevices()\n> - CVE-2026-94281: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XListInputDevices()\n>   class parsing\n> - CVE-2026-94282: Out-of-bounds read in libXi\\'s XI2 enter/leave/focus\n>   cookie conversion.\n> - CVE-2026-109089: libXi XGetDeviceControl Control Type Mismatch Heap\n>   Buffer Overflow\n> - CVE-2026-109090: libXi XGetDeviceControl DEVICE_ENABLE Heap Buffer\n>   Overflow\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0525",
